 "notes": "Fixed in this attempt:\n- Scenario length-range: the XCTL at line 52 now passes WS-BIG as a String of 32767 spaces.\n  WS-BIG is a plain PIC X(32767) item that no generated DTO describes, so rule 14 / #3989 applies.\n  The previous attempt passed an 80-byte CaxbDfhcommarea with LENGTH 32767, which is the harness's\n  \"commarea bytes past what its DTO holds\" divergence.\n\nDefects of the original kept:\n- The RESP of the XCTL at line 52 is never tested (unchecked_responses, field-tested).\n  The report runs whenever control returns, which happens only on failure.\n  Fix: IF WS-RESP NOT = DFHRESP(NORMAL) around the report.\n- WS-BIGLEN = 32767 is outside 0..32763, so mode X (or any mode other than S or L, including a blank\n  one) always fails with LENGERR, RESP2 11.\n  The screen then shows \"XCTL FAILED RESP=22 RESP2=11\".\n  Fix: pass LENGTH(80) with a version-2 COMMAREA.\n- Mode L uses XCTL LENGTH(80) on the 10-byte WS-V1. It passes the 70 bytes of WS-NEIGHBOUR, which\n  CAXB reads as V2-TIER, V2-BALANCE and V2-NOTE.\n  Fix: build a real 80-byte CAV2 COMMAREA.\n- The RECEIVE and the XCTLs at lines 44 and 48 code no RESP. A LENGERR on input longer than 20 bytes\n  abends the task with AEIV, and a PGMIDERR abends it with AEI0.\n  Fix: code RESP on those commands.\n\nFacts contradicted: none found.",
